cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or refer to this software, please cite it as below."
title: "agent-gates: machine-checkable gates for LLM agents"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jafari
    given-names: Sepehr
repository-code: "https://github.com/Aeripsen/agent-gates"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-10-16"
abstract: >-
  Four small, deterministic, tested checks on the edges of a language model, three on its output
  before that output can act and one on tool output before the model reads it: an honesty gate for generated resume text, an eligibility gate on a job-queueing tool
  call, a grounding gate that keeps only claims whose quote is verbatim in the source and lexically
  supports the claim, and an injection gate that flags instruction-shaped text in tool output. Each
  documents the attacks and errors it cannot catch.
keywords:
  - llm agents
  - prompt injection
  - tool use
  - grounding
  - ai safety
